  "notes": "TSH Resources Berhad (Bursa stock code 9059, Yahoo ticker 5126.KL) — Malaysian palm + biomass + wood products integrated operator. December 31 fiscal year-end. Three reportable segments: Palm Products (oil palm cultivation, CPO/PK milling), Wood Products (downstream wood manufacture + forest management unit), and Others (biomass power generation, cocoa trading). Total planted oil palm ~39,000-40,000 ha → ~96-99k acres at × 2.47/1000; expanding to 47-50k ha over next few years. FY2022 included one-off ~RM325M land disposal gain (Indonesian estates) inflating Q3FY22 net profit. Quarterly revenue/net profit/EPS/DPS from KLSE Screener parsing of Bursa Form 8 announcements; annuals cross-checked against TSH integrated annual report 5-year highlights. EBITDA estimated as PBT + finance cost + D&A; FV biological-asset gains/losses under MFRS 141 immaterial vs operating profit. Share count ~1,380M (post bonus issue 2014; ~700M before). Annual history extended back to FY2000 from successive TSH annual reports' 5-year financial highlights tables. Pre-2010 acreage was materially smaller (oil palm planted area grew from ~10k ha in 2000 to ~37k ha by 2010 as Indonesian Kalimantan estates matured); per-period totalAcresK reflects approximate planted oil palm at year-end.",
